{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Oil for the light.</b> It is surprising that the entire passage deals with building needs except for this verse, which is a need of the Table above, and it does not say 'wheat for the showbread' or 'sheep for the daily offerings' or 'wood for the arrangement.' One may answer that all three are building needs: the anointing oil, with which all the vessels of the Mishkan were anointed and consecrated; and incense too, for it is the way of kings that they perfume the house for themselves before they enter it — all the more so before the Holy One, blessed be He. And so we find that through the incense the Shekhinah is seen, as it is written: וכסה ענן הקטרת, and as it is written: כי בענן אראה. And oil for the light, for it is the way of kings to light a lamp before them before they enter the house; and even though He does not need it for light, nonetheless it is honor from above."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:02.278214846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}